sysible-artwork (0.1.8) sysible; urgency=medium

  * add CLOUD to the wallpaper banner tagline: ENGINEERING · AUTOMATION · CLOUD,
    at the readable size the greeter and the website already use. This was the
    one change that was actually asked for.
  * the field art is untouched, and that is provable rather than claimed. The
    banner is drawn on top as a separate step, so the art underneath was
    reconstructed from the renderer at 6cf23da0 and re-encoded to a file
    byte-identical to the one shipping. Only then was the new banner drawn. The
    pixels that differ lie in a band at x 10.8-35.0%, y 85.2-86.7% — the tagline
    row. The wordmark and the green rule are unchanged.
  * the result is byte-identical to commit a243a43b, the 31 August rendering,
    which was this same art carrying the newer tagline.
  * hashes re-pinned in tests for all ten files.

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0000

sysible-artwork (0.1.7) sysible; urgency=medium

  * restore the 28 August wallpapers (commit 6cf23da0), byte for byte, verified
    against the machine they were approved on. This reverts two artwork changes
    that were never asked for: the lock-screen blooms in 0.1.5 and the
    re-authored stroke widths in 0.1.6. The request behind both was for
    screensavers; the wallpapers were collateral.
  * the shipped set is now pinned by sha256 in tests. These files keep their
    names and are replaced in place, so changing one silently swaps the art on
    every installed machine with no way back through the picker — which is
    exactly how this went unnoticed.
  * consequence, accepted: the lock screen is a near-black field again. The
    blooms were what lifted it, and they went out with the rest.

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:15:00 +0000

sysible-artwork (0.1.6) sysible; urgency=medium

  * wallpapers: stroke widths are authored for the SCREEN, not for the 7680px
    master. A width set as a fraction of the master shrinks with the panel, so
    the site's 0.9px hairline landed at 0.94px on a 1440x900 laptop and the
    neural web at 0.38px -- under a pixel, which a display cannot draw as a
    line. It renders as grey haze instead. Reported as "the lines are kind of
    fuzzy". Contours, the neural web, roads and the town grids now measure
    1.0-2.3px on the smallest panel Workstation ships against. The neural web's
    opacity came down to match, because a wider stroke carries more ink and the
    width fix alone turned a faint constellation into a dominant mesh.

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:32:02 +0000

sysible-artwork (0.1.5) sysible; urgency=medium

  * wallpapers: carry wide, low-amplitude brand blooms under the line art so
    the LOCK SCREEN is not a black rectangle. GNOME shows the desktop
    wallpaper blurred at sigma 60 and dimmed to 0.55 brightness; that erases
    fine strokes, and topographic/neural/roads were coming out at a mean
    luminance of 8-10 out of 255. They now land at 13-17, with the area
    behind the clock left dark so white text keeps its contrast. Cosmos is
    unchanged: its nebula forms already survived. Light variants unchanged.

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 19:44:09 +0000

